---
import PageLayout from '../../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import release from '../../../data/release-2026-11-19-alpha.json';

const available = release.availability === 'available';
---

<PageLayout
  lang="en"
  title={`ZIGNOS ${release.release} — ZIGNOS`}
  description={`Release notes for ZIGNOS ${release.release}. Release manifest, zpkg ${release.zpkg.version}, stage3 ${release.stage3.revision}.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">RELEASE · ALPHA</span>
      <h1>ZIGNOS {release.release}</h1>
      <p>{release.build_date}</p>
    </section>

    <div class="prose">
      <div class="notice">
        <strong>stage3 downloads are {available ? 'available.' : 'not yet available.'}</strong>
        {' '}The file names, sizes and SHA-256 values for this release are in the
        stage3 table below; other history is collected in the
        <a href="/en/news/">news list</a>.
        For the latest release information, see <a href="/en/releases/current/">Current release</a>.
      </div>

      <h2>This release</h2>
      <p>
        {release.release} consolidates release information into a machine-readable
        manifest. The website, download page, release notes and installation guide
        all read the same <code>release.json</code>, so package counts, sizes,
        versions and checksums can no longer disagree.
      </p>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat">
          <strong>{release.stage3.package_count}</strong>
          <span>stage3 packages</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <strong>{release.stage3.size_mib} MiB</strong>
          <span>stage3 size</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <strong>{release.stage3.revision}</strong>
          <span>stage3 revision</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <strong>zpkg {release.zpkg.version}</strong>
          <span>Package manager</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Highlights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Release manifest</strong> — generates
          <code>release.json</code> for every build. Records the stage3 SHA-256,
          {release.stage3.package_count} packages and versions, the zpkg / kernel / GRUB
          versions, the size of the base, recipe counts, the build date, source
          commits and boot verification status
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Automatic artifact generation</strong> — in addition to the stage3
          tarball, generates the recipe trees for all channels and the zpkg binary at
          build time, recording their SHA-256 in the manifest
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>zpkg {release.zpkg.version}</strong> — the three channels stable /
          testing / unstable, and <code>zpkg upgrade</code> with diff display,
          build-all-then-install, integrity checks and per-package rollback
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>initscripts r15</strong> — updates <code>/etc/os-release</code> to
          <code>ZIGNOS {release.release}</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Boot verification</strong> — this time BIOS / UEFI / real hardware are
          all <code>{release.boot.bios}</code>. Added a mechanism for
          <code>qemu-test.sh</code> to record results in the manifest automatically
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>stage3</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>File</th><td><code>{release.stage3.filename}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Size</th><td>{release.stage3.size.toLocaleString('en-US')} bytes ({release.stage3.size_mib} MiB)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>SHA-256</th><td><code class="hash">{release.stage3.sha256}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Channel</th><td>{release.channel}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Recipes and toolchain</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Recipes</th><td>{release.recipes.total} ({release.recipes.per_channel} per channel)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Recipes tarball</th><td><code>{release.recipes.filename}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Linux kernel</th><td>{release.kernel.version}-r{release.kernel.revision}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>GRUB</th><td>{release.bootloader.version}-r{release.bootloader.revision}</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Base</th><td>Top level {release.base.top_level} / with dependencies {release.base.closure}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Upgrade</h2>
      <p>
        Existing systems should check the channel before upgrading. This release
        includes an initscripts version bump.
      </p>
      <pre><code>zpkg channel
zpkg upgrade -p
zpkg upgrade</code></pre>
      <p>
        For details on diff display and recovery, see
        <a href="/en/docs/channels/">Release channels</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Boot verification on BIOS / UEFI / real hardware has not been done (<code>not-tested</code>)</li>
        <li>The official signing key is not in operation yet, and artifacts are unsigned</li>
        <li>Bootable images are not included in this manifest's artifacts</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Next</h2>
      <p>
        We will fill in automatic boot verification recording with actual image
        builds, and move forward with signing key operation and bootable image
        distribution. See also the <a href="/en/docs/roadmap/">roadmap</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
